Lars Kecke schrieb:
> 
> Hawkeye-X wrote:
> > What is the best way to kill Asmodeus
> 
> Vorpy (sorry, I like that sword, especially against covetous monsters),
> rubber chicken, stoning grenade, blocking his escape route.

When the current weapon is Grayswandir, the character may well be
lawful, which would make acquiring Vorpal Blade (neutral) a bit
tricky. The other methods are good and reliable.

> > or is it not really necessary?
> 
> You can also bribe him when he first appears. Or leave him alone (the
> last one especially applies to demons summoned by co-racial sacrifice).

The four bribable demon lords (Asmodeus, Baalzebub, Dispater, Geryon)
are lawful and cannot be summoned by coracial sacrifices.

> > I have a +2 Grayswider that doesn't seem to kill him as easily as I
> > thought.
> 
> Well, he teleports away to heal. Follow him.

Or let him follow you - if you change level with him adjacent to you,
he'll come along.

> > I'm a level 16 valkyrie with -25 ac.
> 
> Your AC and your weapon's plus are quite bad for Ghennom.

A double-damage artefact weapon should be better than +2 by now,
agreed. But -25 AC is _very_ comfortable for a Valkyrie in the early
parts of Gehennom. Actually, it's not too difficult for that class to
ascend with such AC.

For _that level_ of Gehennom, i'd consider -10 AC "quite bad".

